cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This repository is an independent computational reproduction. If you use it, please
  also cite the original paper it reproduces (see references below).
title: "LightIN — computational reproduction of a silicon photonic FPGA"
authors:
  - family-names: Das
    given-names: Abhishek
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raar1999/lightin-photonic-fpga-repro"
abstract: >-
  An honesty-first simulation reproduction of the LightIN silicon photonic FPGA:
  unitary/non-unitary matrix multiplication, an Iris unitary neural network, MRM
  wavelength locking, a 4x4 optical switch, and a photonic PUF, plus a coupled-mode-theory
  coupler fitted to the chip's measured crosstalk, a single-theta expressivity analysis,
  and a scattering-matrix-network solver for the recirculating mesh. No fabricated numbers;
  hardware-only measurements are explicitly not reproduced.
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
keywords:
  - silicon photonics
  - photonic FPGA
  - reproduction
  - unitary mesh
  - coupled-mode theory
  - physical unclonable function
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      LightIN: a versatile silicon-integrated photonic field programmable gate array with
      an intelligent configuration framework for next-generation AI clusters
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhu
        given-names: Ying
      - name: "et al."
    journal: "Light: Science & Applications"
    volume: 15
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1038/s41377-026-02209-5
